==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|trousse|lang=fro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/tɹʌs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|trusses}}

# A [[bandage]] and [[belt]] used to hold a [[hernia]] in place.
#* {{quote-book
|year=2008
|author=Lippincott Williams & Wilkins
|title=Professional Guide to Diseases
|chapter=4
|isbn=0781778999
|page=280
|passage=A '''truss''' may keep the abdominal contents from protruding into the hernial sac; however, this won't cure the hernia.}}
# A [[framework]] of beams forming a rigid [[structure]].
# {{architecture}} A [[triangular]] [[bracket]].
# An old English farming [[measurement]]. One truss of straw equalled 36 pounds, a truss of old hay equalled 56 pounds, a truss of new hay equalled 60 pounds, and 36 trusses equalled one load.

